The existing measured absolute grammar supplies prior verbs and exact scalar quantities. The final clause accepts only `Finally, use all the remaining <exact saved description>.` or `Enfin, utilisez tout le reste de <exact saved description>.` / `d’<description>`, case insensitive, horizontal leading/trailing whitespace and optional terminal period. Straight and curly apostrophes are supported. The comma after Finally/Enfin is required. These anchored clauses independently prove final exhaustive intent from all three parts, final marker, all marker and remainder marker. The primary final UTF-16 span selects exactly `remaining` or `reste`.

Exactly two distinct ordered saved steps mention one unique saved ingredient description once each. The first must be a measured absolute use with exact saved unit text, a positive scalar amount and a known scalar total at least the prior amount. The row is proportional and unpackaged, with a recognized existing GroceryUnit mass, volume or culinary bucket. No conversions occur. Extra or repeated references, alternatives, conditionals, ambiguous partial clauses without an independent other-row subject, unknown units/totals, ranges and malformed identities abstain.

Both bindings carry existing `allocationGroup:{id,exhaustive:true,bindingIds:[priorId,finalId]}`. The final carries `allocationGroupId` and `predecessors:[priorId]`. Evidence binds source/content/text revisions, stable row/step identity and exact literal spans. Fresh validation strips supplied bindings and rederives the whole sequence, then checks graph identity and evidence against the supplied proof. Provider flags, equality and group labels confer no authority. The existing projector owns arithmetic and quiet invalidation.

A guarded total correction preserves the measured prior wording and proof when the source and text dependencies remain exact. At basis4/target8, total2 yields prior2/remainder2, total3 yields prior2/remainder4, total1 yields prior2/remainder0, total1/2 yields original readable wording for both. Grocery demand is ingredient-owned. An edit replaces affected proof and downstream dependency evidence. Independent other-row proof must retain identity and eligibility.
